# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  NOVA BACKEND — environment overrides
#  Copy this file to ".env" (same folder) and edit. Everything is optional;
#  with no .env at all you get the LOCAL defaults (127.0.0.1:7777).
#  Switch LOCAL ↔ GLOBAL by editing the values below — no code changes.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── LOCAL (single PC / LAN testing) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave everything commented out. The client is sent to 127.0.0.1:7777, where
# your Project Reboot gameserver hosts the match. Nothing here touches the
# internet, so nothing can use your family's bandwidth or ever charge you.

# ── GLOBAL (friends over the internet, via a free playit.gg tunnel) ───────────
# 1) Run your Reboot gameserver locally (it listens on 127.0.0.1:7777).
# 2) Run playit.gg → it gives you a public address, e.g. nova-abc.playit.gg:45678,
#    that forwards to your local 7777.
# 3) Put THAT public address here so matchmaking hands it to every player:
#NOVA_GAME_SERVER_IP=nova-abc.playit.gg
#NOVA_GAME_SERVER_PORT=45678

# ── MMS websocket URL the client is told to use for matchmaking ──────────────
# LOCAL: leave as-is. GLOBAL (coordinator behind a Cloudflare Tunnel): set to
# your coordinator's public wss URL, e.g. wss://nova.example.com
#NOVA_MMS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:3551

# ── Advanced: multiple gameservers by playlist (Reboot "gameServerIP" style) ─
# Comma-separated "address:port:playlist". A player is routed to the entry whose
# playlist matches; anything else falls back to NOVA_GAME_SERVER_IP/PORT above.
#NOVA_GAME_SERVERS=127.0.0.1:7777:playlist_defaultsolo,127.0.0.1:7778:playlist_defaultduo

# ── P2P SMART MATCHMAKING / AUTO-HOST ELECTION ───────────────────────────────
# The launcher calls GET /nova/api/matchmaking/should-i-host at Play. When this
# is ON, that endpoint runs the smart election:
#     • no server up for the playlist, OR the only match is full / already
#       started (past its join window)           → this player HOSTS a fresh match
#     • a joinable match is up (still in its join window) → this player JOINS it
# The elected launcher spins up + registers the Reboot server, and the MMS
# handler then HOLDS each joiner on the matchmaking screen until that server
# registers (or NOVA_HOST_ELECTION_WAIT_MS elapses, after which the client is
# released rather than hanging forever).
#
# ⚠ Turn this ON for multiplayer via the launcher (the launcher auto-registers
#   the host). Leave it OFF for single-PC manual-inject testing — with it OFF the
#   client is simply sent to the config server (127.0.0.1:7777) after ~5s. A
#   manually-injected Reboot DLL does NOT register itself, so under election a
#   solo manual test would wait out the timeout. Changing this needs a
#   coordinator restart (Config is read once at startup).
#NOVA_HOST_ELECTION=1
# How long a joiner waits for the elected host's server to come up (ms; def 150000).
#NOVA_HOST_ELECTION_WAIT_MS=150000
# How long a freshly-opened match still accepts joiners before it counts as
# "already started" and a new host is elected instead (ms; def 60000).
#NOVA_JOIN_WINDOW_MS=60000
